msgid "AWS Lambda SnapStart configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/snapstart.html[SnapStart] is a "
"snapshotting and restore mechanism reducing drastically the cold startup "
"time of Java functions on AWS.\n"
"This document explains the various settings you can use to leverage this "
"feature.\n"
"It is not a reference documentation on SnapStart, and it will not cover how "
"SnapStart works in details."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enabling / Disabling SnapStart Optimizations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you use the Quarkus AWS Lambda extension, SnapStart optimizations are "
"automatically enabled.\n"
"However, you can enable/disable it explicitly using:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Class Preloading"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Classloading has a huge impact on your function execution time.\n"
"This optimization allows preloading classes during the snapshotting process "
"of SnapStart."
msgstr ""

msgid "The classes to preload are listed in two places:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"extensions can produce a list of classes (using the `io.quarkus.deployment."
"builditem.PreloadClassBuildItem` build item)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"you can add a `src/main/resources/META-INF/quarkus-preload-classes.txt` file "
"listing the classes to preload, such as:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The format is simple: one class per line."
msgstr ""

msgid "Computing the class list"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To compute the list of classes, we recommend deploying your function and "
"setting the `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS` environment variable to `-verbose:class`.\n"
"Then execute your function and retrieve the log (in CloudWatch).\n"
"You should be able to extract the class names using sed/awk or any text "
"editor."
msgstr ""

msgid "Application class list"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Quarkus generates the class list of the classes included in your "
"application (including the classes generated by Quarkus).\n"
"So, you do not have to repeat them in the `quarkus-preload-classes.txt` file."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "You can disable this feature using:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Disable preloading"
msgstr ""

msgid "You can disable the preloading of classes using:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Skipping class initialization"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, when the classes are preloaded, they are also _initialized_, "
"meaning it also resolves the dependent classes.\n"
"You can disable this behavior using:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Client Priming"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Client _priming_ is a technique that allows initializing a client during the "
"snapshotting process, so it's already fully functional during the "
"application runtime."
msgstr ""

msgid "There are two ways to achieve _priming_:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"initialize the client in a `static` block, which, thanks to class preloading "
"will be executed before the snapshot"
msgstr ""

msgid "register a CRaC Resource doing the initialization"
msgstr ""

msgid "(1) can be achieved as follows:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The next section covers (2)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Resource registration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SnapStart uses the CRaC API to allow the application to execute custom code "
"before the snapshotting or during the restoration."
msgstr ""

msgid "TieredCompilation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is also recommended to use _tiered compilation_ when using SnapStart.\n"
"To achieve this, set the `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS` environment property to `-XX:"
"+TieredCompilation -XX:TieredStopAtLevel=1`."
msgstr ""
